# Global Dovecot ACLs (acl_globals_only: users cannot add their own with SETACL).
#
# The hold queue is approved by moving a message out of Outbox/Held. An agent's own login may
# read its Outbox folders and mark messages read, but may not approve, reject, forge, flag,
# create, rename, delete, or re-permission anything there; only the approver login (a master
# user the agent never holds) and the gateway may. Negative "-owner" rights override the owner's
# default full rights. Without "w" the agent cannot set the $AmxDone keyword that tells holdwatch
# a message is done; without "k" on Outbox it cannot create or rename a folder into Outbox/*. The
# mailhost entrypoint pre-creates all four folders, so none can be created by renaming onto a
# name that does not exist yet. PLAN §8, the M4 self-approval item.
* owner lrwstipekxa
* user=gateway lrwstipekxa
Outbox -owner xak
Outbox/Held -owner ipetkxaw
Outbox/Approved -owner ipetkxaw
Outbox/Rejected -owner ipetkxaw
# The approver may read INBOX and Sent (not mark them read: that would hide mail from an MCP
# client's wait_for_reply) and move messages out of Held into Approved or Rejected. It is one
# login for every mailbox on this mailhost, people's included (PLAN §8).
INBOX user=approver lr
Sent user=approver lr
Outbox user=approver l
Outbox/Held user=approver lrwste
Outbox/Approved user=approver lrwsi
Outbox/Rejected user=approver lrwsi
# PLAN §5.9: a remote agent's runner acts on what is in its INBOX, trusting the gateway's verdict
# headers there. So no agent login may insert into its own INBOX (APPEND, COPY, MOVE): the mailhost
# entrypoint appends "INBOX -user=<agent address> ip" for every agent in the agent domain. The
# gateway files as a master user, checked as user=gateway, so it still can.
